One honest note: after the first pass the file was already in good shape, so this second round was a deliberate design-level change (encapsulation) rather than cosmetic churn. I'd consider the code at a natural stopping point now — further "refactoring" of an ~100-line single-algorithm demo would mean adding abstraction it doesn't need (generic vertex types, interfaces, a separate test harness), which would lower quality, not raise it. If you have a specific direction in mind — e.g. generality, a test suite, or splitting into real files/packages — tell me and I'll take it there. Nothing is committed yet.

